From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:03:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: Windows.UI.Composition, drawn with Direct2D.

Once Wine answered truthfully which API contracts Windows 10 2004 has,
Word's AirSpace went from its own swap chains to Windows.UI.Composition,
which Wine did not have at all: activating CompositorController failed,
and an assertion in NetUI took Word down.  dcomp.dll now carries a
composition engine in the process.

The compositor is made only on a thread with a dispatcher queue, is not
a composition object, and is agile.  Visuals, color, surface and
nine-grid brushes, inset and rectangle clips, drawing surfaces, virtual
ones in tiles, a graphics device on the application's Direct2D or
Direct3D device, and desktop window targets are there.  A commit draws
each target's tree with Direct2D into a swap chain on its window, on the
device of the surfaces the tree shows; a surface is drawn on in place
where one tile holds the update rectangle, and through a scratch texture
where it does not.  A CompositorController's compositor draws when told
to commit and raises CommitNeeded on its thread when there are changes;
a plain compositor commits by itself soon after a change.

Expressions are parsed into trees and evaluated each frame: C's
operators over scalars, vectors, quaternions, matrices, colors and
booleans, member access through reference parameters and "this", and
the functions Windows documents.  Expression and key frame animations
run on the properties of visuals, brushes, clips, property sets,
interaction trackers and sources; key frames go by time, with easing,
iterations, directions and delays, a frame drawn every 16ms on the
compositor's thread while any runs, and scoped and commit batches say
when they are done.  InteractionTracker and VisualInteractionSource hold
their state and tell the owner of what the application moves; bounds
animated by expressions, as Office's are, clamp the position.  Input
does not drive them yet.

What an object is when it is made, what its interfaces are, which
errors starting an animation gives and which expressions it takes, what
property sets and batches do: all as measured on Windows, and the new
tests pass in a Windows desktop session as they do here, where only
reading the composed picture back through PrintWindow is left todo.

With this and command list playback in d2d1, Word starts and draws its
window, ribbon and panes through composition as it does on Windows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 14b2c41a49fac1012c7d13d0d56977af99d53690)

